Mavergreen's own, not yet upstream: ld64.lld writes a program's weak binding info sorted by symbol
name, non-weak definitions among the names, as ld64 does. lld (22.1.8, and main as of 2026-10-19)
writes it in address order.

Why: dyld before dyld3, 10.9's dyld-239 among them, coalesces weak symbols across images by walking
every image's weak binding info in step, always advancing the image whose current name is lowest
(ImageLoader::weakBind). An image whose names are out of order is passed over for each name it reaches
after another image has moved beyond it, and the two images keep separate definitions. On 10.9 that
made a type_info defined in a header (weak in every image) differ between a program and its dylibs, so
a catch in one missed an exception of that type thrown in the other; inline functions' static locals
split the same way. Apple's ld64-241.9 sorts by name, and the same program linked by it coalesces.

tests/weak-bind-order-test.sh is the regression test (the table on any host; the coalescing where
x86_64 runs). To offer upstream, with that test's case as an lld lit test.

diff --git a/lld/MachO/SyntheticSections.cpp b/lld/MachO/SyntheticSections.cpp
index 36d1541..09ab858 100644
--- a/lld/MachO/SyntheticSections.cpp
+++ b/lld/MachO/SyntheticSections.cpp
@@ -674,12 +674,28 @@ void WeakBindingSection::finalizeContents() {
   raw_svector_ostream os{contents};
   Binding lastBinding;
 
-  for (const Defined *defined : definitions)
-    encodeWeakOverride(defined, os);
+  // Emit the entries in symbol name order, non-weak definitions among them, as
+  // ld64 does. dyld before dyld3 coalesces weak symbols by walking every
+  // image's weak binding info in step, always advancing the image whose current
+  // name is lowest, so it assumes each image's names are sorted; an image whose
+  // names are not is passed over for every name it reaches after another image
+  // has moved beyond it, and each keeps its own definition.
+  auto sorted = sortBindings(bindingsMap);
+  llvm::stable_sort(sorted, [](const auto &a, const auto &b) {
+    return a.first->getName() < b.first->getName();
+  });
+  std::vector<const Defined *> defs(definitions.begin(), definitions.end());
+  llvm::stable_sort(defs, [](const Defined *a, const Defined *b) {
+    return a->getName() < b->getName();
+  });
+  auto nextDef = defs.begin();
 
-  for (auto &p : sortBindings(bindingsMap)) {
+  for (auto &p : sorted) {
     const Symbol *sym = p.first;
     std::vector<BindingEntry> &bindings = p.second;
+    for (; nextDef != defs.end() && (*nextDef)->getName() <= sym->getName();
+         ++nextDef)
+      encodeWeakOverride(*nextDef, os);
     os << static_cast<uint8_t>(BIND_OPCODE_SET_SYMBOL_TRAILING_FLAGS_IMM)
        << sym->getName() << '\0'
        << static_cast<uint8_t>(BIND_OPCODE_SET_TYPE_IMM | BIND_TYPE_POINTER);
@@ -693,6 +709,8 @@ void WeakBindingSection::finalizeContents() {
     for (const auto &op : opcodes)
       flushOpcodes(op, os);
   }
+  for (; nextDef != defs.end(); ++nextDef)
+    encodeWeakOverride(*nextDef, os);
   if (!bindingsMap.empty() || !definitions.empty())
     os << static_cast<uint8_t>(BIND_OPCODE_DONE);
 }
